  "result": "I fixed it: `Cart.remove` now drops the Widget line, and all the tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:31`, `Cart.remove` matched lines on `line.item.name` instead of `line.item.sku`. `remove('sku-1')` compared the SKU against the name `'Widget'`, found no match, and left the line in the cart.\n\n**Fix:** it now compares against the SKU (`l.item.sku != sku`), the same way `Cart.add` finds existing lines.\n\n**Check:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, meaning only the Gadget line is left. Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest discover`: 6 passed.\n\nNone of the tests cover `Cart.remove`, which is how this bug went unnoticed. I can add a regression test if you want one.",
